      children: "This route is deliberately unremarkable - that's the point. Each concern (retrieval, gateway routing, tracing) lives in its own module, is independently testable, and can be swapped without touching the others. The Next.js route itself is just composition and error handling, which is exactly the amount of responsibility an API route should carry in this architecture."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.h2, {
