    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "A few practices consistently separate maintainable LLM systems from brittle ones. Version prompts explicitly - whether in Langfuse's prompt management, a database table, or a version-controlled file - so a regression can be traced to a specific prompt change rather than an ambiguous \"it got worse recently.\" Keep structured-output schemas as the single source of truth shared between the request payload sent to the model and the validation applied to its response, using something like Zod so the two can never silently drift apart."
